sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bacillus subtilis Turing wavenumber at 16 µm (Holocene detail scale) — MorphoEval overall 90.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 closes the pass-1 gaps. The bulk Schnakenberg field now reaches the nonlinear regime and its radial peak is 16.00 µm (mode 12). Dispersion slopes on the Turing band match the discrete Laplacian at Pearson r=0.99998 and RMSE=0.00110. The ocellus rays are darker (contrast 0.82) and the GIF scores cv_sim_similarity 89.4 against the Korinna 2019 micrograph at 520 px and 12 frames. The specimen ridge count is 43 against the model circumference mode 72, so that comparison is deliberately not a self-copy. Equal-diffusion ablation still suppresses the pattern. Age is 0 Ma (chronoseries 1/1); the scale change versus the 10 µm tier center is k ratio 0.624. Gates after this pass are met, so pass 3 was not run. Nanopubs were not signed. Overall 90.1/100 (faithfulness 89.8, reproducibility 90.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 9e461936b246cc6182241d6552184d9a372036e6; environment: python 3.12. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 89, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/bacillus_subtilis_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 9e461936b246cc6182241d6552184d9a372036e6, image/gif, 1753746 B, 520×520 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 782aa13d8c10ae33efaf1f999007beda333338240beac59dd64612d2927ba815 (sha256 782aa13d8c10ae33efaf1f999007beda333338240beac59dd64612d2927ba815), spec_fingerprint 8c9e9022c4aac6bcf41bc35b63530ab7c52c0841a7764224d5403753680be47b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 8c9e9022c4aac6bcf41bc35b63530ab7c52c0841a7764224d5403753680be47b; artifact_sha256: 782aa13d8c10ae33efaf1f999007beda333338240beac59dd64612d2927ba815; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bacillus_subtilis_turing_wavelength_s0/bacillus_subtilis_ocellus_specimen.jpg=94a0bad84960d16e..., datasets/bacillus_subtilis_turing_wavelength_s0/bacillus_subtilis_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=4cb53436d064578e...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite critical wavenumber from a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Kawasaki 1997, Golding 1998, and Ben-Jacob 2000 model Bacillus subtilis colony branches with reaction-diffusion at colony scale. | The Korinna 2019 micrograph is an eye-shaped B. subtilis colony and carries no scale bar.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics a=0.084, b=0.916, diffusion ratio 9.20. Linear k_star gives 16.02 µm. The nonlinear bulk field on the 192 µm square peaks at radial mode 12, wavelength 16.00 µm, std(u)=0.27. | Dispersion goodness-of-fit on modes n=8..20: Pearson r=0.99998, RMSE=0.00110. | Kinematic front at R=183.3 µm draws m=72 rays spaced by 16 µm. Specimen ridge count on the micrograph is 43.; transfer_boundary: Colony-scale branching papers supply organism context. They are not a measurement of a 16 µm wavelength.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that any cited paper measured a 16 µm pigment stripe in B. subtilis. | Does not claim the ray ocellus is a disk-bounded solution of the bulk PDE, or that its branch count fits the micrograph (43 versus 72).." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: High-pass ridge count on the specimen is 43, not the model mode 72. Do not read m=72 as a fit to the photograph; the micrograph has no scale bar.",
            "remediation needed: The animated ocellus is still a kinematic front at the selected wavelength, not an integration of the Schnakenberg PDE inside a growing disk, so it does not reproduce the irregular dendritic branches of the micrograph." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.901"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (loop 3130 pass 2 primary assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

